# data-models-relationships

Core Entity Models:

1. Inmate Records
- Links to active cases and bond details
- Phone number and contact associations  
- Status tracking (active/released)
- Location history references

2. Case Management
- Bond compliance requirements
- Check-in schedule and verification rules
- Geographic restrictions and allowed zones
- Agent assignments

3. Location Verification 
- GPS coordinates with accuracy radius
- IP-based location fallback data
- Timestamp and verification method
- Linked compliance events

4. Bond Records
- Amount and payment status
- Compliance requirements
- Geographic boundaries
- Agent oversight assignments

Key Relationships:
- Inmates -> Cases (1:N)
- Cases -> Bond Records (1:1)
- Inmates -> Location History (1:N) 
- Cases -> Compliance Events (1:N)
- Agents -> Cases (N:M)

Relevant Files:
- app/main.py: Core entity definitions and relationships
- app/db.py: Data model schemas
- app/geo.py: Location model integration

Importance Score: 95
The data models and their relationships form the critical foundation for the warrant service and bond compliance tracking system. The interconnected nature of inmates, cases, locations and compliance events enables the core business functionality.

